  "casePolicy": [
    "Compare the original target criterion and original grammar independently.",
    "Each case declares allowed tuples/interpretations before model outputs. Equivalent grammatical corrections are not restricted to a single string, but novel alternatives require evidence-based review against the same frozen intent.",
    "Do not add or remove an accepted alternative after observing results to raise the score. Record proposed changes and preserve the original grade; a new version requires newly sealed confirmation families.",
    "A field-label policy mismatch is auxiliary; known original form error, correction equivalence and abstention are different dimensions.",
    "Unavailable transport/parser/no-response is not an English grammar fail or a fabricated critical error; it remains a nonpass in the frozen denominator.",
    "Score only visible factual explanations. Raw model reason errors and app-forced abstention are separate diagnostics.",
    "A critical flag requires the corresponding visible bad approval/reversal/role swap/invented intent evidence; uncertainty alone does not establish a critical claim.",
    "An unspecified permissible alternative goes to blind adjudication under preregistered rules; do not auto-fail on string difference or auto-pass on fluent wording."
  ],
